:RaceOrEthnicity rdfs:comment "Although race is a social rather than biological construct, it can be an (albeit imperfect) proxy for certain genetic traits. Because European ancestry is a risk factor for AF (Marcus et al., 2010; Roselli et al., 2018), this may explain why incidence of AF is higher among White people than in other racial groups (Dewland et al., 2013; Volgman et al., 2019)." ,
                              "The racial/ethnic categories proposed in the AFMO are not intended to be prescriptive or exhaustive. They can be adapted based on what is relevant for the target population." ;
                 rdfs:label "Race or ethnicity" ;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ethnicity is a term for the ethnic group to which people belong. Usually it refers to group identity based on culture, religion, traditions, and customs. In some contexts, it is a “politically correct” term equivalent to the word “race,” which may have pejorative associations." ,
                                                                  "Race is a social construct used to group people. Race was constructed as a hierarchal human-grouping system, generating racial classifications to identify, distinguish and marginalize some groups across nations, regions and the world. Race divides human populations into groups often based on physical appearance, social factors and cultural backgrounds." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :RaceOrEthnicity ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "Ethnicity is a term for the ethnic group to which people belong. Usually it refers to group identity based on culture, religion, traditions, and customs. In some contexts, it is a “politically correct” term equivalent to the word “race,” which may have pejorative associations." ;
   rdfs:isDefinedBy "Oxford Refence https://www.oxfordreference.com/display/10.1093/oi/authority.20110803095759525, accessed 09 July 2026."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :RaceOrEthnicity ;
   owl:annotatedProperty <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "Race is a social construct used to group people. Race was constructed as a hierarchal human-grouping system, generating racial classifications to identify, distinguish and marginalize some groups across nations, regions and the world. Race divides human populations into groups often based on physical appearance, social factors and cultural backgrounds." ;
   rdfs:isDefinedBy "The National Human Genome Research Institute. https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary/Race"
 ] .


:SleepApnoeaStatus rdfs:comment "Sleep apnoea status in a monitored person (present or absent)" ;
                   rdfs:label "Sleep apnoea status" .


:SmokingStatus <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "UMLS:C0453996"@en ;
               <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> "Tobacco smoking behaviour"@en ;
               rdfs:comment "A person's cigarette (tobacco) smoking behaviour."@en ;
               rdfs:label "Smoking status" .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource :SmokingStatus ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:comment ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "A person's cigarette (tobacco) smoking behaviour."@en ;
   rdfs:isDefinedBy """https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/nhis/tobacco/tobacco_recodes.htm#anchor_1557516509294 and the New Zealand Ministry of Health https://www.health.govt.nz/our-work/preventative-health-wellness/tobacco-control/tobacco-control-information-practitioners/definitions-smoking-status.

- Smoker (a.k.a current smoker): a person who has smoked more than 100 cigarettes (including hand rolled cigarettes, cigars, cigarillos etc) in their lifetime and has smoked in the last 28 days. Includes daily and non-daily/social smokers.
- Non-smoker: composed of two groups: former smoker and never smoker.
   - Former smoker: a person who has smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime but has not smoked in the last 28 days. The international convention is to treat someone as an ex-smoker once they have been smokefree for one month (at least 28 days).
   - Never smoker: a person who has not smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime and does not currently smoke.

Dagfinn et al. (2018) noted that there is reduced risk of AF among former smokers compared to current smokers, but further research is needed to determine if the risk at some point reaches that of never smokers."""
 ] .


